IFQ - DISPLAY CONDITIONAL STATE

CALLER. Subject to the current caller access policy.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
IFQ - DISPLAY CONDITIONAL STATE

CALLER. Subject to the current caller access policy.

Syntax:
    IFQ

Displays the active IF tree, current level first. For example IF FTT means
the current third level is false and its two parent levels are true. IF
None means there is no active IF.

It reports flow-control state without changing file permissions or wheel
privileges.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
